From: RTL9617C Maintainers <dev@openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: nand: bbt: avoid GENMASK shift-out-of-bounds across word boundary

When a BBT status entry straddles a BITS_PER_LONG boundary (e.g., 3-bit
entries at offs=62 or offs=63 on 64-bit), offs + bits_per_block - 1
exceeds BITS_PER_LONG - 1, causing GENMASK() to shift by a negative /
wrapped exponent (triggering UBSAN shift-out-of-bounds and failing to
clear the upper bits of pos[0] on arm64).

Clamp the upper bit index for pos[0] to BITS_PER_LONG - 1; the remaining
bits in pos[1] are already masked and updated immediately below.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/bbt.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/bbt.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 #define pr_fmt(fmt)	"nand-bbt: " fmt
 
+#include <linux/minmax.h>
 #include <linux/mtd/nand.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 
@@ -113,7 +114,8 @@ int nanddev_bbt_set_block_status(struct
 	if (entry >= nanddev_neraseblocks(nand))
 		return -ERANGE;
 
-	pos[0] &= ~GENMASK(offs + bits_per_block - 1, offs);
+	pos[0] &= ~GENMASK(min_t(unsigned int, offs + bits_per_block,
+				 BITS_PER_LONG) - 1, offs);
 	pos[0] |= val << offs;
 
 	if (bits_per_block + offs > BITS_PER_LONG) {
